          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Birth and Early Life</strong><br>\nScott Joplin, born around 1868 in Texas, was an African American composer and pianist, acclaimed for his ragtime compositions. He was born into a musical family, and his talent was evident from a young age when he taught himself to play the piano.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ragtime Music and Early Compositions</strong><br>\nJoplin dedicated himself to the development of ragtime, a music genre that combined African American musical styles with European forms and melodies. His early works, like \"Maple Leaf Rag,\" became the genre's defining compositions and catapulted Joplin to fame.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The 'King of Ragtime'</strong><br>\nDubbed the 'King of Ragtime,' Joplin's music became synonymous with the ragtime era. His compositions were celebrated for their complex bass patterns and syncopated melodies, which represented a significant contribution to American music.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
